<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main class="container page-content" style="max-width: 780px;">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-text">
      <h1>Vigilentia Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Ephemeral code handling, zero permanent storage, and BYOK encryption.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card privacy-card">
    <section class="privacy-section">
      <h2>1. Code Diffs & LLM Processing</h2>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li><strong>Ephemeral Diff Transmission:</strong> Diffs are sent directly to the Google Gemini API to analyze for bugs and security vulnerabilities.</li>
        <li><strong>Zero Permanent Code Storage:</strong> Source code is never stored in our database or on disk. Once posted, diffs are immediately discarded from memory.</li>
        <li><strong>Model Training Protection:</strong> Requests made with your API key are governed by Google GenAI terms and not used for model training.</li>
        <li><strong>Prompt Injection Defense:</strong> Diffs and guidelines are treated as untrusted data boundary inputs.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section">
      <h2>2. Bring-Your-Own-Key (BYOK) Encryption</h2>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li><strong>AES-256-GCM Encryption:</strong> Stored with unique 96-bit initialization vectors and authentication tags.</li>
        <li><strong>Master Key:</strong> Kept in the server environment (<code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>), never in the database.</li>
        <li><strong>In-Memory Decryption Only:</strong> Keys are decrypted only for the duration of the review job.</li>
        <li><strong>Last 4 Characters Visible:</strong> Only the last 4 characters are ever displayed.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section">
      <h2>3. Custom Style Guides & RAG Embeddings</h2>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li><strong>pgvector:</strong> Rule embeddings (768-d) stored in PostgreSQL with pgvector.</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-Tenant Isolation:</strong> Retrieval queries strictly filter by <code>installation_id</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section">
      <h2>4. Complete Data Deletion on Uninstall</h2>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li>Automated <code>installation.deleted</code> webhook immediately deletes the tenant record.</li>
        <li>Cascading database foreign keys permanently wipe encrypted keys, style rules, embeddings, reviews, and comments.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section">
      <h2>5. Authorization & Sessions</h2>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li>GitHub OAuth with httpOnly and secure session cookies.</li>
        <li>CSRF validation on all state-changing endpoints.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
